PURPOSE of /kernel/power-management/rapl/powerclamp
Description: Test if clamping of power works.
Author: Erik Hamera <ehamera@redhat.com>

RAPL = Running Average Power Limit

Check RAPL functions. It checks power consumption for idle and 0 - 49% clamped full load.
The energy consumption should be higher for lower clampings.

The error range is 20% now - it is __NOT__ wisely choosen magical number emerging
from intel's datasheets or something like that. It __IS__ just wild guess which
should suppress false alarms due to started daemons and other fluctuations. Feel
free to change it if your guess is better, than mine.

It works on RHEL 7 and RHEL 6 both, because it isn't using perf, but reads directly
from /proc. Therefore overflow must be checked, which complicates timing. Therefore
energy.sh from this test isn't compatible with energy.sh from my older tests!

